==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|pt}} {{term|παραλληλεπίπεδος||with parallel surfaces|lang=grc}}, from {{term|παράλληλος||parallel|lang=grc}} + {{term|επίπεδος||plane|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˌpærəˌlɛləˈpaɪpɪd/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|geometry|lang=en}} Solid figure, having six faces, all [[parallelogram]]s; all opposite faces being similar and [[parallel]].
#* ''A cuboid is a rectangular '''parallelepiped'''.''

====Derived terms====
* [[parallelepipedic]]

====Hyponyms====
* [[cuboid]]

